  "notes": "Disney-era teen-pop with an electronica surface over pop-rock bones: 118–128 straight, backbeat on 2&4. The harmonic claim is unusually precise and is what separates this model from the rest of the teen bench — the documented cell of the 2003 single is a two-chord vamp with an added 2nd/7th rather than functional movement (G-sharp-maj7 to E in B major, i.e. vi and IV), so `maxChords` drops to 2, the vamp carries top weight, the sevenths and ninths outweigh the triad and the harmonic rhythm leans on `vamp` and `2_bars_per_chord`. Drums are three quoted facts: a \"driving\" 16th hat (pinned base, high fill density), \"kick on all four in the chorus\" (density 3–4 with syncopation pulled right down), and \"a rain-stick/white-noise riser as the transition device\", which is the riser lane in the percs. The melody is \"narrow (F-sharp3–B4) and speech-like in verse, opening to a long-held chorus note\", which is the 54–71 register with a low density, and the \"hypnotic arpeggiated synth pattern\" is the counter running as an `arp` at a high ratio. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and the bass numbers — \"synth bass pulsing 8ths under the pad, sidechained feel against the kick\" gives a rhythm and no values.",
